cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "evalmut: mutation testing for evaluation suites"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
  Citing the archived release rather than the repository pins the exact code
  a result came from, which is the whole point of the tool.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Erik
    family-names: Hill
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-5912-967X"
    email: erik@erikhill.dev
repository-code: "https://github.com/egnaro9/evalmut"
url: "https://erikhill.dev"
abstract: >-
  Mutation testing for evals. Injects declared defects into the system under
  test and reports which of the suite's checks stay green. A surviving mutation
  is a measured hole in the eval, not an error. Operators are mined from
  documented defects rather than authored for coverage, and an operator that
  cannot establish its mutant's polarity declines rather than guessing.
keywords:
  - mutation testing
  - evaluation harnesses
  - software testing
  - LLM evaluation
  - test suite validity
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
